  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The current I flowing through the given circuit will be _____&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0119_1786c4e5fc0f.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 136px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Here all resistors are in parallel, so the equivalent circuit can be redrawn as shown below.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0119_5729ba57156a.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 168px;\" /></p><p>As identical resistances are in parallel, so equivalent resistance is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Now, current through circuit is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}